{
  "rose_format": 1,
  "name": "runner",
  "version": "1.0",
  "files": [
    {
      "name": "runner.crim",
      "source": "# runner 1.0 - run other Crim+ files from a Crim+ program\n# Use it with:   use runner\n# Example:       if run_crim with \"exercises/one.crim\" is 1, then do:\n#                    say \"It ran! It printed: \", then crim_output\n#                anything else do:\n#                    say \"It stopped with: \", then crim_error\n#                end if\n# Needs a Crim+ that has the \"run file\" statement. Each file runs in its own copy of Crim+, so it can't change your\n# variables, and a file that never finishes is stopped after a time limit (10 seconds unless you say otherwise).\n# The file has to end in .crim and stay inside your program's folder (the same rule as other files).\n#\n# Run a file. Each of these gives back 1 if it ran with no error, otherwise 0:\n#   run_crim with \"one.crim\"\n#   run_crim_input with \"one.crim\" and \"Sam\"        answers the file's questions (ask). Give a list to answer\n#                                                   several questions, one answer per item.\n#   run_crim_within with \"one.crim\" and 5            stops it after 5 seconds\n#   run_crim_expect with \"one.crim\" and \"Hello\"      1 only if it ran with no error AND printed that same text\n#                                                   (blank space at the very start or end is ignored). To check\n#                                                   several lines, read the expected text from a file into a variable.\n# After any of them, you can look at:\n#   crim_output     what it printed\n#   crim_error      the error message, or \"\" if there wasn't one\n#   crim_timed_out  1 if it was stopped for taking too long, otherwise 0\n#   crim_exit_code  0 for a normal finish\n# Helper variables and helper instructions inside this module start with rc_ so they won't clash with yours.\n\nset rc_output to \"\"\nset rc_error to \"\"\nset rc_timed_out to 0\nset rc_exit_code to 0\n\ninstruction to rc_run using path and answers and limit:\n    run file path with input answers within limit seconds into rc_result\n    set rc_output to output of rc_result\n    set rc_error to errors of rc_result\n    set rc_timed_out to timed_out of rc_result\n    set rc_exit_code to exit_code of rc_result\n    give back ok of rc_result\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to run_crim using path:\n    give back run rc_run using path and \"\" and 10\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to run_crim_input using path and answers:\n    give back run rc_run using path and answers and 10\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to run_crim_within using path and limit:\n    give back run rc_run using path and \"\" and limit\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to run_crim_expect using path and expected:\n    set rc_ran to run rc_run using path and \"\" and 10\n    if rc_ran is 0, then do:\n        give back 0\n    end if\n    set rc_want to expected, then \"\"\n    set rc_want to trim of rc_want\n    set rc_got to trim of rc_output\n    if rc_got is rc_want, then do:\n        give back 1\n    end if\n    give back 0\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to crim_output:\n    give back rc_output\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to crim_error:\n    give back rc_error\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to crim_timed_out:\n    give back rc_timed_out\nend instruction\n\ninstruction to crim_exit_code:\n    give back rc_exit_code\nend instruction\n"
    }
  ]
}
